From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fuzzlang: emit internal diagnostic ID on stderr

After TextDiagnosticPrinter renders each diagnostic, emit an extra line

    DiagID: <N>

carrying the internal diagnostic enum value (Info.getID()). This lets
downstream tools classify diagnostics unambiguously without string-matching
on the localized message text.

In recent LLVM (17+), `TextDiagnosticPrinter::OS` is a `raw_ostream &`, not
a pointer — we use `OS << ...` and `OS.flush()` accordingly. Two emission
points are patched:

  - the invalid-location branch (command-line diagnostics);
  - the primary post-emitDiagnostic path.

Developed against LLVM 19.1.7. See scripts/patches/README.md for manual
derivation notes if the anchor lines have drifted in your checkout.

---
 clang/lib/Frontend/TextDiagnosticPrinter.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/clang/lib/Frontend/TextDiagnosticPrinter.cpp b/clang/lib/Frontend/TextDiagnosticPrinter.cpp
--- a/clang/lib/Frontend/TextDiagnosticPrinter.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/Frontend/TextDiagnosticPrinter.cpp
@@ -124,6 +124,10 @@ void TextDiagnosticPrinter::HandleDiagnostic(DiagnosticsEngine::Level Level,
         /*IsSupplemental=*/Level == DiagnosticsEngine::Note,
         DiagMessageStream.str(), OS.tell() - StartOfLocationInfo,
         DiagOpts->MessageLength, DiagOpts->ShowColors);
+    // Fuzzlang: emit the internal diagnostic ID even for command-line /
+    // invalid-location diagnostics so downstream parsers can classify them
+    // unambiguously without string-matching the localized message.
+    OS << "DiagID: " << Info.getID() << "\n";
     OS.flush();
     return;
   }
@@ -144,6 +148,12 @@ void TextDiagnosticPrinter::HandleDiagnostic(DiagnosticsEngine::Level Level,
                              DiagMessageStream.str(), Info.getRanges(),
                              Info.getFixItHints());

+  // Fuzzlang: emit the internal diagnostic ID for programmatic classification.
+  // Placed after the rendered diagnostic body so existing parsers continue to
+  // see the unchanged header/body; the DiagID line follows as extra info and
+  // the DVCR verifier's regex `^DiagID:\s*(\d+)\s*$` picks it up.
+  OS << "DiagID: " << Info.getID() << "\n";
+
   OS.flush();
 }
